<title>GERMANY: TABLE-OECD German GDP forecasts for 1997, 1998.</title>
<headline>TABLE-OECD German GDP forecasts for 1997, 1998.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris-based Organisation for</p>
<p>Economic Co-operation and Development published the following</p>
<p>forecasts for Germany on Tuesday.</p>
<p>						     1996   1997   1998</p>
<p> Private consumption			    1.3    1.0    2.0</p>
<p> Government consumption			 2.4    1.1    1.1</p>
<p> Total fixed investment			-0.8    1.6    4.2</p>
<p>    Construction				 -2.7   -0.5    0.7</p>
<p>    Machinery and equipment		   2.4    4.9    9.3</p>
<p> Stockbuilding				   -0.3    0.1    0.1</p>
<p> Total domestic demand			  0.8    1.3    2.5</p>
<p> Net exports					0.6    1.0    0.3</p>
<p>    Exports of goods and services	   4.9    8.4    7.5</p>
<p>    Imports of goods and services	   2.6    4.8    6.6</p>
<p> GDP at market prices			   1.4    2.2    2.8</p>
<p> GDP deflator				     1.0    1.2    1.1</p>
<p> Private consumption deflator		 1.9    1.7    1.8</p>
<p> Unemployment (in millions)		   4.0    4.3    4.2</p>
<p> Unemployment (percent of labour force)  10.3   11.1   10.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures represent seasonally adjusted percentage changes at annualised rates except where otherwise stated. Stockbuilding and net exports data refer to contributions to changes in GDP as a percent of real GDP in the previous period.</p>
<p>--Janet Northcote, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
